artifacts/
!artifacts/model.joblib
# Everything else in artifacts/ stays ignored (intermediate/scratch output);
# model.joblib is force-added and tracked despite the directory rule above.
# It's what api/recommend and api/cold-start need to serve anything -- without
# it a fresh deploy answers "No trained model found. Run python train.py
# first." on both, which is exactly what happened on the first Vercel deploy
# of this fix. results.json and static/embedding.json come from the same
# training run and were already committed; this closes the one piece that
# was inconsistent with them. Re-run train.py and re-add this file (2.6MB)
# whenever the model changes -- it does not update itself.
